        answer: "Garden apartments, mid rise buildings, and mixed income properties across Duval, Clay, and St. Johns counties qualify as like-kind replacement property when they are held for investment rather than as a primary residence. The property does not need to match the class of the relinquished property, only its like-kind and investment character.",
